  "id": "eyehand-coordination",
  "term": "eye–hand coordination",
  "definition": "Eye–hand coordination is the ability to link visual information with hand and arm movements so actions are smooth, accurate, and well timed. It depends on synchronized control of the eyes and hands, with gaze usually directed to a target before the movement, helping with tasks such as catching, grasping, or aiming at a target.",
